MLLM description: The Redhead duck is characterized by its distinctive reddish-brown head and neck, contrasting with a dark gray body. Its beak is long, slightly curved, and predominantly white with a black tip. The eyes are bright yellow with a black pupil. The duck's size is medium, with a robust build and a relatively short tail. It has a calm demeanor, often seen floating on water with minimal movement. The unique identifying trait is the combination of the reddish-brown head and neck against the dark gray body, which sets it apart from other duck species.
